# Keep credentials and build junk out of the build context.
#
# This file is load-bearing, not tidiness. The build used to `git clone` the
# repo from inside the image, which only ever saw tracked files. It now copies
# from the local build context, so anything gitignored-but-present on disk is
# fair game — and application-local.yml sits under src/main/resources, which
# `COPY src/ src/` pulls in wholesale. Without the exclusions below, Maven
# would package real MQTT/Postgres/admin credentials into the jar.

# Secrets and local config.
# Scoped patterns, not a bare *.properties: Docker ignore patterns don't cross
# '/', so *.properties would only ever catch the root anyway, while
# .mvn/wrapper/maven-wrapper.properties MUST survive — the wrapper reads it to
# know which Maven to download, and the build dies without it.
**/application-local.*
**/application-dev.*
**/application-prod.*
**/application-testcontainers.*
.env
/config/

# Build output
target/

# VCS and tooling
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github
.idea
.vscode
.claude
.aider*

# Runtime artefacts from local runs
logs/
spring-client-*/
hs_err_pid*
replay_pid*

# Docs — not needed to build, and changing them shouldn't bust the cache
*.md
Modelfile
docker-compose*.yml
Dockerfile
